.SH DESCRIPTION
The single-box control plane inside a site's air gap (Sprint 14a). A
release bundle enters only as the verified copy of
.B robodr\-release
import and only with a passing, signed
.B entry report
for exactly that bundle. Units enrol with their TPM (endorsement-key
certificate, credential activation, certified keys, a quote) and two
operators. Rollouts go ring by ring
.RB ( lab " \(-> " canary " \(-> " ring\-1 " ...),"
each stage a deployment signed by the depot and approved by the operator
quorum of its ring; the next stage exists only after every unit of the
current one reported its items installed and healthy after the soak, and a
failing report halts the rollout. Sealed content keys are re-wrapped for
each enrolled unit of a stage, never for another. Units fetch their pack
over mutual TLS or receive a per-unit media pack. With leases (Sprint 14b)
each accepted report renews the unit's site lease.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B entry scan
On the entry station (no depot configuration): verify the bundle as
.B robodr\-release
would against the trust file and the pinned roots, check every RPK's SBOM
(CycloneDX) against the vulnerability database
.RB ( robodr\-vulndb/1 ),
and write the report
.RB ( robodr\-entry\-report/1 )
and its signature (the trust file's
.B entry
role). The verdict is
.B fail
when a vulnerability at or above
.B \-\-fail\-on
(default high) is listed; a report lives at most 30 days.
.TP
.B init
Once: create the state directory, the site's trust anchor (the trust file
under the pinned roots and site), the unit CA certificate, the TLS server
key and certificate (with
.BR serve ),
an empty database and its anchor.
.TP
.B trust update
Advance to a rotation of the trust file.
.TP
.B import
Import a bundle with its entry report. Refused: no report, a report for
another bundle, site or RPK list, an expired or failing report, a report
not signed by an entry key; a revoked or below-floor RPK; a chain gap,
replay or equivocation; RPKs sealed to depot keys the trust file does not
list
.RB ( robot.depot.import_refused ).
.TP
.B enrol begin
A fresh nonce for unit
.I U
(which the trust file must assign to a ring). On the unit:
.BR "robodr\-seal enrol\-request \-\-nonce" .
.TP
.B enrol verify
Check the unit's request: the EK certificate chains to a TPM vendor CA
whose SHA-256 the trust file lists
.RB ( ek_ca_certs );
the AK, UWK and unit identity key are TPM-resident (attributes) and
certified by the AK; the UWK is bound to the site's policy authority,
erase epoch and (with leases) lease key; the quote over the nonce matches
the signed policy's PCRs. Writes the credential challenge
.RB ( TPM2_MakeCredential
to the EK for the AK's name).
.TP
.B enrol finish
The unit's answer
.RB ( "robodr\-seal enrol\-activate" ):
only the TPM holding both the EK and the AK can recover the secret. One
wrong answer closes the enrolment.
.TP
.B enrol approve
An operator signs the activated enrolment; at two distinct operators the
unit is enrolled
.RB ( robot.depot.unit_enrolled ;
a refusal at any step is
.BR robot.depot.enrolment_refused ).
.TP
.B enrol export
The unit's client certificate (issued by the depot's unit CA for its TPM
identity key) and the CA certificate, for its
.B depot
section.
.TP
.B unit revoke
Operator quorum: the unit is served nothing more and nothing is wrapped
to it.
.TP
.B inventory
Units (ring, state, attestation, last report, installed items, erased),
rollouts and deployments, and whether the depot is locked, as JSON.
.TP
.B rollout create
A rollout of RPK digests over
.B \-\-stages
(rings in ascending order, starting at
.B lab
or
.BR canary ;
a production ring needs a canary stage first), with
.B \-\-batch
(default 1),
.B \-\-soak\-s
(default 600),
.B \-\-max\-failures
(default 0),
.B \-\-validity\-days
(default 30) and optionally only some units
.RB ( \-\-unit ).
Makes the first stage's deployment.
.TP
.B rollout advance
The next stage, only when the current one passed.
.TP
.B rollout resume|abort
Operator quorum: resume a halted rollout (its stage is deployed again under
a new sequence number and approved again) or abort it.
.TP
.B deploy approve
An operator signs a deployment; at the quorum of its ring it is active.
.TP
.B report import
A unit's signed report from media
.RB ( "robodr\-deliverd report \-\-out" ).
A failure beyond
.B \-\-max\-failures
halts the rollout
.RB ( robot.depot.rollout_halted ).
.TP
.B pack
Write unit
.IR U 's
media pack (its newest active deployment, the trust file, the RPKs it
targets, with only that unit's wrapped keys; its lease).
.TP
.B serve
The LAN server (mutual TLS, rustls with its safe default protocol
versions). A client is a
unit only if its certificate chains to the depot's unit CA
.B and
its public key is an enrolled unit's identity key; that unit gets its own
pack
.RB ( "GET /v1/pack" )
and may post its own reports
.RB ( "POST /v1/report" ,
answered with its lease). No request names a unit.
.TP
.B reanchor
Operator quorum: accept a database the anchor check locked
.RB ( robot.depot.locked ),
with the deployment sequence raised to at least
.I N
so no sequence number is reused.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.I /etc/robodr\-depot/depot.json
.RB ( robodr\-depot\-config/1 ,
unknown members refused; example in
.IR /usr/share/doc/robodr/examples/depot.example.json ):
.BR site ", " depot_id ,
the pinned
.BR roots ,
.BR state_dir ,
.B keys
.RB ( signing :
the trust file's depot key;
.BR wrap :
the X25519 depot wrapping key;
.BR lease :
the P-256 lease key;
.BR ca :
the unit CA key),
.B enrolment
.RB ( policy_authority ", " ek_cas ", " ek_intermediates ,
.BR allow_without_tpm " (default false), " cert_days ),
and optionally
.B lease
.RB ( lifetime_s :
TPM powered-on time,
.BR reboots ),
.B serve
.RB ( listen ", " server_name ", " max_connections ,
.BR max_connections_per_source " (default 4), " deadline_s ;
a peer must complete the TLS handshake within 10 s),
.B anchor
(an NV counter of the depot's TPM:
.BR tcti ", " index ", " work_dir ", " tools_dir )
and
.B findings
(the box's agentd spool).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/robodr/depot/
State (0700 robodr\-depot): database, trust anchor, store, deployments,
unit records and reports, TLS server key, and
.I depot.lock
(one writer at a time: the server per request, an operator command for its
run; the other waits at most 60 seconds).
.TP
.I /etc/robodr\-depot/keys/
The depot's keys (0700 robodr\-depot).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 ok, 1 refused or error, 2 usage.
.SH SYSTEMD UNIT
.B robodr\-depot.service
(installed disabled, for the depot box) runs
.B serve
as
.B robodr\-depot
without capabilities,
.BR ProtectSystem=strict ,
the TPM only through
.BR DevicePolicy=closed " and " DeviceAllow=/dev/tpmrm0 .
Run operator commands as the same user:
.B runuser \-u robodr\-depot \-\- robodr\-depot \-\-config /etc/robodr\-depot/depot.json
.IR ... .
.SH LIMITS
Keys are files (the design's HSM or depot-TPM keys are not implemented).
One depot per site: no high availability. Tested with software TPMs
(swtpm) and EK certificates from swtpm's local CA only, never a vendor
EK CA or a hardware TPM. The quote is checked against the signed policy's
PCR values, not against an event log. A lease bounds a unit's powered-on
time and reboots, not wall time.
